{"id":"rs_2883c815-77c3-9d32-9e86-510028d8c554","summary":[{"text":"I'll write a SPARQL query to sample distribution URLs.

QLever's regex support is uncertain. I'll first probe counts for schema:DataDownload and schema:distribution. Then I'll sample URLs with a LIMIT clause to avoid huge results. Extension classification will be done client-side from those samples.

I can extract file extensions directly in SPARQL using REPLACE and REGEX. URLs without extensions will remain unchanged, which I can detect to label them as unknown. Aggregating thousands of URLs in QLever is feasible, but fetching distinct URLs for local classification is another option.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning","status":"completed","encrypted_content":""}

